{"duration_api_ms":9817,"stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"83fc9bce-453e-4329-b36d-de3060ede99e","total_cost_usd":0.0011627,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":723,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":1535,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":1172},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":723,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1535,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"cache_creation_input_tokens":723,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":723},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"modelUsage":{"claude-haiku-5-5":{"inputTokens":1266,"outputTokens":1783,"cacheReadInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationInputTokens":723,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.0011627,"contextWindow":1000000,"maxOutputTokens":128000,"thinkingTokens":1398,"cacheCreationEphemeral5mInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationEphemeral1hInputTokens":723,"canonicalModel":"claude-haiku-5-5","provider":"firstParty","costBasis":"list"}},"permission_denials":[],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","fast_mode_disabled_reason":"sdk_opt_in_required","subagent_stats":{"spawned":0,"requested":{"background":0,"foreground":0,"unset":0},"started_in_background":0,"max_depth":0,"spawned_by_subagents":0,"completed":0,"failed":0,"killed":{"parent":0,"user":0,"system":0},"refused":{"depth_limit":0,"concurrency_limit":0,"budget":0},"by_type":{}},"safety_stops":0,"is_error":false,"num_turns":1,"subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"**Short answer:** Yes, potentially, but only indirectly and only if the fund's exemptive relief and portfolio conditions permit it.\n\n**Mechanism:** ETF-class authorized participants redeem creation units in kind, receiving portfolio securities rather than cash. The RIC can choose which low-basis lots to deliver, and under IRC §852(b)(6) it generally doesn't recognize gain on in-kind distributions in redemption. Because the classes share one portfolio, fewer realized gains reduce the taxable distributions allocated across all classes, including mutual fund classes.\n\n**Limits:**\n- Benefit depends on ETF-class redemption volume and available lots; it isn't guaranteed.\n- Mutual fund class cash redemptions can still force sales that realize gains.\n- Lot selection is constrained by basket rules and the need to keep the portfolio representative.\n- Cross-class fairness rules under Rule 18f-3 and the fund's multi-class plan still apply.\n- Relief varies by fund, so the mechanism must be verified against each fund's own order and prospectus.","ttft_ms":6768,"type":"result","duration_ms":8345,"uuid":"89f40268-b963-442d-9e68-945d8946efec","ttft_stream_ms":493,"time_to_request_ms":88,"first_content_frame_ms":493,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0,"credential_expires_at":"2026-11-28T06:36:39.484Z"}
